  "protocol": "Constants fixed before evaluation. 24 separate-seed six-asset 1000-session synthetic histories, four variants, 30-session query, 20-session horizon, stride 20, six spaced neighbours, candidate outcomes strictly mature before query start. Shared date intersection and coverage retained. Exploratory 5000-resample seed-cluster bootstrap. Generators inherited from relation experiments; linked-drift embeds an artificial state/outcome link.",
  "limitations": [
    "Small-basket persistence loses asset-label identities and can map different networks to identical diagrams.",
    "Correlation distances omit absolute volatility, drift, time ordering and nonlinear dependence beyond rank association.",
    "Unshrunk short-window correlations are noisy; no persistence significance intervals are estimated.",
    "Winsorization can suppress genuine systemic shocks.",
    "W2 is not bottleneck distance and does not inherit the same dimension-free max-error bound.",
    "Fixed 70/30 channels and 50/50 H0/H1 weights are design choices, not validated optimum.",
    "Ripser/GUDHI are unavailable here; independent GF2 persistent-rank and SciPy assignment oracles were used.",
    "No real-market alpha evidence; bootstrap intervals are exploratory and unadjusted for multiple comparisons."
  ]
